<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Divided succession and partible inheritance</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Divided succession and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/partible-inheritance">partible inheritance</a> describes the practice of dividing a realm among a ruler's heirs rather than passing it intact to one successor. It frequently produced civil war and fragmentation. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> was split among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a>'s sons, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> broke into rival branches, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> divided among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s relatives.</p></div>
